body:
### Tested versions

Reproducible in 4.7 stable, 4.7.2 stable

### System information

Godot v4.7.2.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9636) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-13700K (24 threads) - 63.78 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)

### Issue description

When writing a gdshader, setting a variable to LIGHT_AREA_DIFFUSE_MULTIPLIER or LIGHT_AREA_SPECULAR_MULTIPLIER in ```void light()``` hangs the editor when saving the shader and eventually throws a 10,000+ line error ending with ```ERROR: servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shader_rd.cpp:414 - Condition "variant_stages.is_empty()" is true.```

Arithmetic including these values and one float and the equals ```=``` assignment operator produces this error. Using +=, -=, *=, and /= do NOT produce this error. Wrapping these values in a new vec3 also works. Equations with vec3 do NOT produce this error, even with floats.

### Steps to reproduce

In new project, create a new gdshader.
Uncomment a line and save (or wait for autosave)

```gdshader
shader_type spatial;

void vertex() {
}

void fragment() {
}

void light() {
    // Any of these lines will trigger the error - uncomment a line to test

    vec3 value = 1.0 * LIGHT_AREA_DIFFUSE_MULTIPLIER;
    //vec3 value = LIGHT_AREA_DIFFUSE_MULTIPLIER.rgb;
    //vec2 value = LIGHT_AREA_DIFFUSE_MULTIPLIER.rg;
    //float value = LIGHT_AREA_DIFFUSE_MULTIPLIER.g;
    //DIFFUSE_LIGHT = LIGHT_AREA_DIFFUSE_MULTIPLIER;

    // These lines do NOT trigger the error

    //vec3 value = vec3(LIGHT_AREA_DIFFUSE_MULTIPLIER);
    //vec3 value = vec3(1.0) * LIGHT_AREA_DIFFUSE_MULTIPLIER;
    //vec3 value = 1.0 + vec3(1.0) * LIGHT_AREA_DIFFUSE_MULTIPLIER;
    //DIFFUSE_LIGHT += LIGHT_AREA_DIFFUSE_MULTIPLIER;

    // Accessing and swizzling only r or x channel works

    //vec3 value = LIGHT_AREA_DIFFUSE_MULTIPLIER.rrr;
    //vec2 value = LIGHT_AREA_DIFFUSE_MULTIPLIER.rr;
    //float value = LIGHT_AREA_DIFFUSE_MULTIPLIER.r;
}
```

